    "body": "Hi @ajnart ,\n\nIndeed. My default dashboard is open on my MacBook (integration is beszel and Patchmon)\n\nRegularly I open homarr on my mobile, few apps but Beszel and Docker integration. \n\nBeszel is set to live (I guess, what other options are available?)\n\nI just did it again, same result\nSo I need to let my integrations go?\n\nOr is the memory allocation of node.js the issue? 1.5G memory for the Container should be more than sufficient. \n\n\n<--- Last few GCs --->\n\n07:34:05\n\n07:34:05\n[16023:0x7f940f7be000] 41475678 ms: Scavenge (interleaved) 757.6 (767.2) -> 757.6 (778.2) MB, pooled: 0 MB, 18.13 / 0.00 ms  (average mu = 0.978, current mu = 0.222) allocation failure; \n\n07:34:05\n[16023:0x7f940f7be000] 41477084 ms: Mark-Compact (reduce) 764.6 (778.2) -> 764.6 (770.7) MB, pooled: 0 MB, 607.98 / 0.00 ms  (+ 713.7 ms in 111 steps since start of marking, biggest step 79.6 ms, walltime since start of marking 1406 ms) (average mu = 0.96\n\n07:34:05\nFATAL ERROR: Reached heap limit Allocation failed - JavaScript heap out of memory\n----- Native stack trace -----\n\n07:34:08\nAborted (core dumped)\n\n07:34:08\nNext.js exited with code 134, restarting in 1s...\n\n07:34:09\n\u25b2 Next.js 16.2.10\n\n07:34:09\n- Local:         http://ea4c22eb9faa:3000\n\n07:34:09\n- Network:       http://ea4c22eb9faa:3000\n\n07:34:09\n\u2713 Ready in 0ms\n\n07:34:10\n2026-07-23T05:34:10.746Z info: \u2705 WebSocket Server listening on ws://localhost:3001 module=\"websocketMain\"\n\n07:34:15\n2026-07-23T05:34:15.304Z info: Starting schedule of cron job. module=\"cronJobs\" name=\"analytics\"\n\n07:34:15\n",
